WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.849
A drone operations center turns individual flights into a governed program.

00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:11.599
It coordinates mission intake, approval, roles, scheduling, aircraft, payloads, live support,

00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:15.257
data products, safety, privacy, security, and compliance.

00:00:15.257 --> 00:00:19.961
Strong governance defines purpose, scope, authority, exclusions, handoffs, escalation,

00:00:19.961 --> 00:00:22.052
and pilot command responsibility.

00:00:22.052 --> 00:00:27.801
Facilities and systems should support secure storage, battery safety, planning, communication,

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:30.415
maintenance, data protection, and recovery.

00:00:30.415 --> 00:00:35.641
Scheduling combines current airspace, weather, location, crew readiness, aircraft status,

00:00:35.641 --> 00:00:39.300
payload fit, emergency options, and data requirements.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:44.004
Fleet management tracks each asset, battery, configuration, defect, repair,

00:00:44.004 --> 00:00:45.572
and lifecycle decision.

00:00:45.572 --> 00:00:50.276
Live support prioritizes safety information, clear communication, action-oriented status,

00:00:50.276 --> 00:00:54.980
emergency coordination, and decision logging without replacing the pilot.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:59.161
Data workflows preserve provenance, metadata, originals, privacy, confidence,

00:00:59.161 --> 00:01:00.729
and specialist review.

00:01:00.729 --> 00:01:05.956
The goal is reliable, safe, lawful, privacy-conscious, and accountable operation,

00:01:05.956 --> 00:01:08.047
not simply more flights.

00:01:08.047 --> 00:01:13.273
Continuous improvement comes from maintenance evidence, after-action review, audit trails,

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:18.500
and a culture willing to pause unsafe or unjustified missions.
